      *                                                                         
      *       If you need to access information on another production           
      *       group, (collection) you must set the desired group here.          
              10  BZXOJNA0-In-PackageSet         Pic  X(08).                    
      *                                                                         
      *       Logging is performed at two places in the interface.              
      *       -After input convert, the input qualification is                  
      *        displayed. For Insert and Update also the data items             
      *        are displayed.                                                   
      *       -Before output convert, the retrieved data is displayed.          
      *        The output data is only displayed when data is found             
      *        (i.e. -Return-OK) and input qualification is a read              
      *        (Get first/next, select or count) For count, only the            
      *        count is displayed.                                              
      *                                                                         
      *       Options for logging:                                              
      *       -Logging-No No logging is performed. This is the default.         
      *       -Logging-Dump Unformatted dump.                                   
      *       -Logging-Format All items are prefixed by their name,             
      *        but no new line between the items.                               
      *       -Logging-Format-Line All items are prefixed by their name,        
      *        each item on a separate line.                                    
      *                                                                         
